# L §5.9 Keyed bands: "band b[k in IDX](x: T): U holds one table per key ... Rows are written b[k]: [lo, hi) = …,
# the table checks run per key, and the band is called b[k](x)."  The ends take the band with its key:
# band_hi(b[k], x).  For class c1 the row [0, 10) gives 1; for c2 the row [0, 20) gives 5 and its upper end is 20.
# held: (L §8.2) "a row whose span has a start and no end ..., band rows included, read at a law date after the
# cut K": the law date is after the model's on, so every open-ended row read is listed.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
index classes = [c1, c2]
band b[k in classes](n: int): int
input x: int

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  b[c1]: [0, 10) = 1
  b[c1]: [10, inf) = 2
  b[c2]: [0, 20) = 5
  b[c2]: [20, inf) = 6
  x = 12

ask q1: b[c1](x), b[c2](x), band_hi(b[c2], x) law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: (2, 5, 20)
  held: b[c1] row [10, inf) (v), read for 2026-06-30
  held: b[c2] row [0, 20) (v), read for 2026-06-30
  held: x = 12 (v), read for 2026-06-30
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
